Tesla this week updated its app with native <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ipad/">iPad</a> and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-duo/">iPhone Duo</a> support, adapting its vehicle and home energy controls for larger displays.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/tesla-app.jpg" alt="" width="1672" height="941" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1072112" /><br/>
<br/>
Previously, &zwnj;iPad&zwnj; users could install the iPhone app, but it lacked native support with a layout designed for the larger screen. The new interface essentially uses two columns, with navigation and controls on the left and a larger visualization of the vehicle or home on the right.<br/>
<br/>
Tesla designer Alex Guichet <a href="https://x.com/AlexGuichet/status/2112933588132155719">announced the update</a> on October 21, sharing screenshots and confirming support for Android tablets and foldable devices as well. The release arrives ahead of the &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj;'s launch on Friday, October 23.<br/>
<br/>
